    "question_text": "Explain any four Fundamental Rights guaranteed by the Indian Constitution.",
    "max_marks": 10,
    "answer_key_text": "The Indian Constitution guarantees six Fundamental Rights: Right to Equality (Art 14-18), Right to Freedom (Art 19-22), Right against Exploitation (Art 23-24), Right to Freedom of Religion (Art 25-28), Cultural and Educational Rights (Art 29-30), Right to Constitutional Remedies (Art 32).",
